        {
          "type": "modopedia:text",
          "x": 2,
          "y": 16,
          "width": 96,
          "line_height": 9,
          "text": "The basic workflow uses a canvas, pen, ink bottle, and compass. They are one system: the pen reads the offhand ink, the canvas stores the glyphs, and the compass helps draw"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "boundaries."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• Canvas: a placeable, editable surface that can be packed into an item or wand.\n• Pen: the main-hand painter; brush size and step come from PenProperties."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• Mana ink: the offhand source of color and the gyromancy:mana effect.\n• Compass: draws a radius-controlled circle or arc and can store a pen."
    },
    {
